Bug found by tools/spike_drill.py (seed 7, 200,000 events), fixed in ingest_gate/gate.py.
Reproduce both sides on identical inputs:  python3 tools/bot_window_regression.py --events 200000 --seed 7
  first version (client-time window):  268 of 195,877 clean events flagged as bot
  current (server-time window):          0 of 195,877
(out/bot_window_regression.json; the first version lives on as ClientTimeWindowGate in that tool.)

Cause: the bot-rate window was keyed on client time. One event whose client clock was a
year ahead entered the visitor's window and never aged out, so the next 3 page views from
that (human) visitor tripped the 4-in-1-second rule.

--- a/ingest_gate/gate.py   (pre-fix)
+++ b/ingest_gate/gate.py
@@ def _bot_check(self, ev, client: datetime, flags):
         if ev["type"] == "page_view":
-            window = self._pv_times[visitor]
-            window.append(client)
-            while window and ms_between(client, window[0]) > BOT_BURST_WINDOW_MS:
-                window.popleft()
+            now = parse_ts(ev.get("received_at")) or client
+            window = self._pv_times[visitor]
+            window.append(now)
+            while window and abs(ms_between(now, window[0])) > BOT_BURST_WINDOW_MS:
+                window.popleft()

Regression test: tests/test_gate.py::test_skewed_client_clock_does_not_poison_bot_window
